{"id":"states-a-value-the-page-prints-no-state-for-is-not-taken","path":"inferences/roland-sc8850-01/states-a-value-the-page-prints-no-state-for-is-not-taken.json","unitId":"roland-sc8850-01","state":"standing","level":"investigating","why":"no model has been rendered and compared with the unit","verdict":null,"standing":"unmodelled","rounds":3,"madeAt":"2026-09-19T04:52:17+00:00","madeBy":"backup/what-a-two-state-byte-does-above-one.py, backup/write-the-printed-states-inference.py, backup/above-a-longer-printed-list.py, backup/add-round-two-to-the-printed-states-inference.py, backup/the-three-state-list-and-four-more-types.py, backup/add-round-three-to-the-printed-states-inference.py","about":{"scope":"unit","class":null,"types":["01 00","01 03","01 10","01 11","01 21","01 22","01 50","01 73","04 01","04 02","04 05","11 06"],"addresses":["40 03 03","40 03 04","40 03 05","40 03 06","40 03 07","40 03 08","40 03 09","40 03 0B","40 03 0D","40 03 0E"],"checkedOnUnits":[]},"title":{"names":[{"name":"Stereo-EQ","page":216,"document":"roland-sc-8850-owners-manual-en"},{"name":"Humanizer","page":216,"document":"roland-sc-8850-owners-manual-en"},{"name":"Overdrive","page":216,"document":"roland-sc-8850-owners-manual-en"}],"more":9,"parameters":[],"parametersMore":0,"document":"roland-sc-8850-owners-manual-en"},"printedTypes":[{"type":"01 00","name":"Stereo-EQ"},{"type":"01 03","name":"Humanizer"},{"type":"01 10","name":"Overdrive"},{"type":"01 11","name":"Distortion"},{"type":"01 21","name":"Auto Wah"},{"type":"01 22","name":"Rotary"},{"type":"01 50","name":"Stereo Delay"},{"type":"01 73","name":"Lo-Fi 2"},{"type":"04 01","name":"GTR Multi 2"},{"type":"04 02","name":"GTR Multi 3"},{"type":"04 05","name":"Bass Multi"},{"type":"11 06","name":"OD / AutoWah"}],"supersededBy":null,"retractedBecause":null,"claim":"An effect parameter whose page prints a list of states takes no byte that is not one of them, and what it does instead is nothing: the parameter goes on sounding the state it was already in. The store is not what refuses -- it keeps every seven-bit value and reads it back, 02 for a write of 02 -- so whatever drops the value sits between the store and the sound. Read on five two-state slots across three of the effect map's high bytes, where nought against one is audible by 11.74 to 15.49 dB of level and one against two, one against 127 and nought against two are all null -- fifteen pairs whose two settings sit between 2.94 dB under and 0.27 dB over the yardstick those settings' own repeats set, against the 6 dB a verdict here has to clear, and none of which moves the level by more than 0.02 dB. The last of those three pairs is the one that decides it: four of the five slots power up in the second state, so a byte that reached the state they power up in would have made nought against two as loud as nought against one. Three printed lists of different lengths agree -- a two-state corner holds at the 1 it had, a three-state amp table and a five-state width both hold at the 0 they had. Those three were all asked on slots that power up at the first entry, where holding what they had and folding to the first are one number, so every length this page prints was then asked again on a slot that powers up inside its own list: a three-state filter selector and a four-state amp table that power up at 1, and a five-state width inside a multi-effect that powers up at 2. Each was asked one past its top three times over -- standing at nought, standing at the value it powers up in, and standing at its last printed state -- and the three readings that a longer list leaves standing each predict a different two of those three to be audible. All nine are null, between 3.79 dB under and 0.87 dB over the yardstick their own settings' repeats set, while the nine in-range pairs of the same three slots are audible by 16.08 to 38.17 dB over theirs. None of the three moves again further up: nought against 127 and the last printed state against 127 are null on each. Eight of the fifty-four slots printed `00/01` now carry it, over eight types including a delay line, a distortion and three guitar multi-effects, each audible at nought against one by 25.66 dB or more and null at nought against two. And the four slots the page prints `00/7F` are not a longer or shorter case of this but a different thing entirely: each was swept over the whole byte with the type reloaded before every take, so what comes back is a function of the byte alone -- the slow rotor from nought to 63 and the fast one from 64 to 127 -- while a slot printed `00/01` returns two different states for the one byte 2 depending on which state it was standing in. No map from a byte to a state does both.","named":null,"whyNotNamed":"There is nothing here to name. This is what the machine does with a value it has no state for, not a structure that processes a signal, and calling it a bound test or a table lookup would assert which of the two it is -- which is the one thing about it these measurements cannot reach.","adds":"Each cited record says what one slot did at the settings it was asked at. None of them says what happens to a value the page has no state for, because each on its own has at least two readings that fit it: the runs that swept past a printed list all reset and reloaded the type between settings, which put the parameter's loaded value and its standing value in the same place, and the one slot anybody had looked at past its list powers up at 0, where folding to the first state, returning the loaded value and keeping the current one are three names for the same number. What is added is the pair that pulls them apart -- nought against two, written in that order with nothing reset in between, on slots that power up at 1 -- and the reading of all of them together as one rule rather than as a habit of one type. Round two adds the shape that lets one slot answer alone. A list of more than two states has three predecessors worth standing in -- nought, the value the type loads, and the last printed state -- and asking one past the top from each of them separates keeping the current state from returning the loaded value, from folding to the first, and from clamping to the last, without putting two slots side by side to do it. Round three closes the last list length the page prints and takes the reading to eight slots over eight types, and it reads a refutation out of records that were already published: the two spellings cannot be one map from the byte to a state, because one of them is such a map and the other is not.","refutedBy":"A slot whose page prints a list of states, asked from one of them at a value outside the list, coming back audible. Cheapest on a slot that powers up in a state it is not being written from: on this unit that is any of the four asked here at nought against two, and the same pair on a printed list longer than two would extend it further. It would also be refuted by a slot where the store does not read back what was written, because then the refusal is the store's and this claim is about the wrong thing.","couldHaveBeenRefutedBy":null,"whatItWouldChange":["A renderer given a MIDI file that writes 2 to a two-state effect parameter must leave the parameter alone. Setting it to the second state is what every reading of the byte short of this one implies, and it is wrong in the one direction that is audible: the parameter is left wherever the file last put it, which after a type change is the value the type loads.","inferences/roland-sc8850-01/width-the-byte-halves-the-printed-table.json reads its own three settings past the fifth as returning the first entry, and now says that its slot also powers up there and that its takes cannot tell the two apart. Which of them it is, is this claim's, and the answer is neither: the parameter holds what it held, which in a run that reloads the type between settings is the same number."],"grounds":{"measurements":[{"file":"data/units/roland-sc8850-01/contrast/40-03-04-humanizer-nought-and-one.json","within":"contrast/40-03-04-humanizer-nought-and-one.json","keys":["values","audible","setting_read_back"],"values":[[0,1],true,[{"setting":0,"reads":"00","took":true},{"setting":1,"reads":"01","took":true}]]},{"file":"data/units/roland-sc8850-01/contrast/40-03-04-humanizer-one-and-two.json","within":"contrast/40-03-04-humanizer-one-and-two.json","keys":["values","audible","setting_read_back"],"values":[[1,2],false,[{"setting":1,"reads":"01","took":true},{"setting":2,"reads":"02","took":true}]]},{"file":"data/units/roland-sc8850-01/contrast/40-03-04-humanizer-one-and-the-top.json","within":"contrast/40-03-04-humanizer-one-and-the-top.json","keys":["values","audible","setting_read_back"],"values":[[1,127],false,[{"setting":1,"reads":"01","took":true},{"setting":127,"reads":"7F","took":true}]]},{"file":"data/units/roland-sc8850-01/contrast/40-03-04-humanizer-nought-and-two.json","within":"contrast/40-03-04-humanizer-nought-and-two.json","keys":["values","audible","setting_read_back"],"values":[[0,2],false,[{"setting":0,"reads":"00","took":true},{"setting":2,"reads":"02","took":true}]]},{"file":"data/units/roland-sc8850-01/contrast/40-03-09-auto-wah-nought-and-one.json","within":"contrast/40-03-09-auto-wah-nought-and-one.json","keys":["values","audible","setting_read_back"],"values":[[0,1],true,[{"setting":0,"reads":"00","took":true},{"setting":1,"reads":"01","took":true}]]},{"file":"data/units/roland-sc8850-01/contrast/40-03-09-auto-wah-one-and-two.json","within":"contrast/40-03-09-auto-wah-one-and-two.json","keys":["values","audible","setting_read_back"],"values":[[1,2],false,[{"setting":1,"reads":"01","took":true},{"setting":2,"reads":"02","took":true}]]},{"file":"data/units/roland-sc8850-01/contrast/40-03-09-auto-wah-one-and-the-top.json","within":"contrast/40-03-09-auto-wah-one-and-the-top.json","keys":["values","audible","setting_read_back"],"values":[[1,127],false,[{"setting":1,"reads":"01","took":true},{"setting":127,"re