[0,2],false,true,false,-33.07,-35.16,0.021,"00","02"]},{"file":"data/units/roland-sc8850-01/contrast/40-03-06-delay-feedback-mode-nought-and-one.json","within":"contrast/40-03-06-delay-feedback-mode-nought-and-one.json","keys":["values","audible","conclusive","reset_before_each_setting","by_stimulus[stimulus_name=struck_kit].across_setting_residual_db","by_stimulus[stimulus_name=struck_kit].same_setting_residual_db","by_stimulus[stimulus_name=struck_kit].across_setting_level_db","setting_read_back[setting=0].reads","setting_read_back[setting=1].reads"],"values":[[0,1],true,true,false,-9.65,-35.77,0.275,"00","01"]},{"file":"data/units/roland-sc8850-01/contrast/40-03-06-delay-feedback-mode-nought-and-two.json","within":"contrast/40-03-06-delay-feedback-mode-nought-and-two.json","keys":["values","audible","conclusive","reset_before_each_setting","by_stimulus[stimulus_name=struck_kit].across_setting_residual_db","by_stimulus[stimulus_name=struck_kit].same_setting_residual_db","by_stimulus[stimulus_name=struck_kit].across_setting_level_db","setting_read_back[setting=0].reads","setting_read_back[setting=2].reads"],"values":[[0,2],false,true,false,-39.99,-39.05,0.013,"00","02"]},{"file":"data/units/roland-sc8850-01/contrast/40-03-06-gtr-multi-3-wah-switch-nought-and-one.json","within":"contrast/40-03-06-gtr-multi-3-wah-switch-nought-and-one.json","keys":["values","audible","conclusive","reset_before_each_setting","by_stimulus[stimulus_name=struck_kit].across_setting_residual_db","by_stimulus[stimulus_name=struck_kit].same_setting_residual_db","by_stimulus[stimulus_name=struck_kit].across_setting_level_db","setting_read_back[setting=0].reads","setting_read_back[setting=1].reads"],"values":[[0,1],true,true,false,-0.55,-40.61,7.836,"00","01"]},{"file":"data/units/roland-sc8850-01/contrast/40-03-06-gtr-multi-3-wah-switch-nought-and-two.json","within":"contrast/40-03-06-gtr-multi-3-wah-switch-nought-and-two.json","keys":["values","audible","conclusive","reset_before_each_setting","by_stimulus[stimulus_name=struck_kit].across_setting_residual_db","by_stimulus[stimulus_name=struck_kit].same_setting_residual_db","by_stimulus[stimulus_name=struck_kit].across_setting_level_db","setting_read_back[setting=0].reads","setting_read_back[setting=2].reads"],"values":[[0,2],false,true,false,-38.03,-37.53,-0.039,"00","02"]}],"documentRows":[{"file":"documents/roland-sc-8850-owners-manual-en/effect-list.json","rows":["01 00 Low Freq, 200/400, 00/01","01 00 Hi Freq, 4k/8k, 00/01","01 00 M1 Q, 0.5/1.0/2.0/4.0/9.0, 00/01/02/03/04","01 03 Drive Sw, Off/On, 00/01","01 21 Polarity, Down/Up, 00/01","01 22 Speed, Slow/Fast, 00/7F","04 01 OD Sw, Off/On, 00/01","04 05 OD Sel, Odrv/Dist, 00/01","04 05 OD Amp, Small/BltIn/2-Stk, 00/01/02","11 06 AW Pol, Down/Up, 00/01"]}],"eraPriors":[{"claim":"A parameter of this period whose page prints a short list of states is an index into a table, and the write path tests it before it stores it.","why":"A handful of printed states against a byte that carries a hundred and twenty-eight is an index, and an index read without a bound test walks off the end of its table into whatever follows it. A machine that has to survive a MIDI file written by anybody tests the value instead, and the cheapest thing to do with one that fails is nothing.","wouldBeWrongIf":"A value past the list reached a state at all -- clamped to the last, folded to the first, or reaching something not on the list. Two of those were asked for and neither happened."}],"community":[]},"alternatives":[{"reading":"The engine reads the byte as nought against not-nought, so every value from 1 up reaches the second state.","candidate":null,"standing":false,"ruledOutBy":"Nought against two is null on all five slots, and four of them -- 01 03 40 03 04, 01 21 40 03 09, 04 01 40 03 0B, 11 06 40 03 0E -- power up in the second state. Under this reading that pair is the two states against each other and would have read as loud as nought against one did, which on those four is 11.74 to 15.49 dB of level over a yardstick 33.1 to 39.8 dB down. The store read the 2 back as 02 in every one of them, so it is not a clamp on the way in. A longer list refutes it on one pair of its own: the four-state amp table of 01 10 reads 1 against 3 -- both of them not nought -- audible by 28.48 dB over its own yardstick, where this reading has them in one state.","equivalent":false,"separatedBy":null},{"reading":"A value past the list folds back to the first state.","candidate":null,"standing":false,"ruledOutBy":"The two-state corners of 01 00 power up in the second state, and every value from 2 to 127 reads where the second state reads -- the low corner's half-power point at 315 Hz against the first state's 200 Hz. The reading held only because the one slot it was first noticed on, the five-state width, powers up at 0, where folding to the first state and keeping the current one are the same answer. It now falls on one slot at a time. Standing at the value it powers up in, neither longer list moves when a byte past its top arrives -- 0.59 dB and 0.38 dB over their own yardsticks -- while nought against that same value is audible on both.","equivalent":false,"separatedBy":null},{"reading":"A value past the list puts the parameter back to the value the type loads it with.","candidate":null,"standing":false,"ruledOutBy":"Nought against two is null on the four slots whose loaded value is 1. The contrast writes the pair in order with no reset between, so the parameter is standing at 0 when the 2 arrives; under this reading it would have gone to 1 and the pair would have been audible. It is not. Every run that had asked this before reset and reloaded the type between settings, which put the loaded value and the standing value in the same place and is why the two readings had never come apart. And on the two longer lists, standing at nought: a byte past the top leaves them there -- -2.86 dB and 0.87 dB over their own yardsticks -- where this reading sends them to the 1 and the 2 their types load, which are audible against nought by 36.68 and 16.08 dB.","equivalent":false,"separatedBy":null},{"reading":"A value past the list is clamped to the last state.","candidate":null,"standing":false,"ruledOutBy":"The five-state width reads 5, 64 and 127 at the width of state 0, not of state 4: band for band they are within 0.06 dB of state 0 while the four real states stand 3.46 to 10.31 dB away from it. The three-state amp table of 04 05 reads its value 3 on state 0's profile in all three of the records that asked it -- 21 to 27 of 113 bands outside their own repeat floor and at worst 5 times it, against 104 to 110 bands and 48 to 532 times it for either real state. Asked directly, from nought, on two lists whose last state is audible against nought by 30.46 and 19.36 dB: one past the top returns null on both, and so does the top of the byte.","equivalent":false,"separatedBy":null},{"reading":"The engine reads the bottom bit of the byte.","candidate":null,"standing":false,"ruledOutBy":"One against two is null on all five slots: the two settings sit between 2.31 dB under and 0.13 dB over the yardstick those settings' own repeats set, against the 6 dB a verdict has to clear, and the level moves under 0.02 dB. Under this reading it is the two states against each other. The four-state amp table refutes it twice over: 1 against 3 share a bottom bit and are audible by 28.48 dB, and 3 against 4 differ in one and are null.","equivalent":false,"separatedBy":null},{"reading":"The value is dropped on its way to the engine rather than ignored when the engine reads it -- the write path tests it, or the parameter is read through a table lookup that has no row for it.","candidate":null,"standing":true,"ruledOutBy":null,"equivalent":true,"separatedBy":{"observable":"Where in the path the byte stops. Nothing that leaves the sockets reports it.","predicts":{"dropped on the way in":"the parameter goes on sounding what it had","ignored on the way out":"the parameter goes on sounding what it had"},"sensitivity_here":"Not applicable: the two predict the same sound and the same read-back, which is 02 for a write of 02 either way.","margin":1,"why_not_separable":"Both put the same number in the store and the same state in the engine. Separating them needs the code, and this project measures a machine from outside it."}}],"reproduces":null,"models":[],"charts":[],"examples":[],"extra":[{"key":"why the control is in the run","text":"Four of the five verdicts wanted here are nulls, and a null from a chain that was not routed that evening is the same null as one from a byte that was not taken. So nought against one was taken again on every slot rather than carried from the run three days before that established it. It came back at 11.938, 11.740, 15.490, 11.931 and 11.936 dB against that run's 11.92, 11.73, 15.50, 11.93 and 11.95 -- the same comparison, within two hundredths of a decibel."}],"slug":"unlisted-settings","documents":[{"id":"roland-sc-8850-owners-manual-en","title":"SC-8850 Owner's Manual","publisher":"Roland Corporation","copyright":"1999","printing":"00-7-A3-31N","language":"en","pagesRead":0,"pages":256}]}
